    "durationMs": 340546,
    "finalText": "The URL shortener is complete and fully verified. Here's what I built:\n\n**Stack**: Rails 8.0.2 (API-only) on Ruby 3.4.3, PostgreSQL via `DATABASE_URL`, Puma on `0.0.0.0:8000`.\n\n**Implementation**\n- `db/migrate/..._create_links.rb` — `links` table with non-null `url`, `code` (unique index), `clicks` defaulting to 0\n- `app/models/link.rb` — validates URL is an absolute http/https URI with a non-empty host, code matches `[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{4,20}` and is unique; generates 8-char codes from a SecureRandom-sourced alphabet when omitted\n- `app/controllers/links_controller.rb` — all four endpoints, atomic `increment_counter` for exact click counting, duplicate-code 409 handling including a race-safe retry on `RecordNotUnique`, plus a lenient fallback that accepts JSON bodies even without a JSON content-type\n- `app/controllers/application_controller.rb` — malformed JSON and record-not-found rescue to JSON 422/404\n- `start.sh` — `db:prepare` then serves in the foreground; README documents startup and the API\n\n**Issues found and fixed along the way**\n- Bundler resolved `json` 3.1.0, which broke ActiveSupport 8.0's JSON parse/generate (`quirks_mode` keyword removed) — pinned Rails to exactly 8.0.2 and `json` to 2.x\n- `URI.parse(\"http://\")` yields an empty-string host that passed my first validation — now rejects no-host URLs\n- Removing the Solid gems/kept dev config clean, and cleared dev host authorization so any Host header works\n\n**Verified by HTTP tests**: 201/409/422/404 paths, boundary code lengths, `http://` with no host rejected, redirects with `Location` matching exactly, clicks incrementing precisely once per request, listing in creation order with correct totals, `application/json` content types, full data and click-count persistence across three server restarts, `db:prepare` creating a fresh database, and `sh /workspace/start.sh` working from any directory. Rubocop reports no offenses, and the test server has been stopped so port 8000 is free."
  }
